# ⚠️  INERT IN PRODUCTION — nginx does not read this file.
#
# napnix.in is served by nginx on the VPS, not by Netlify or Cloudflare Pages.
# `_headers` is a Netlify / Cloudflare Pages convention; it ships into dist/ and
# sits in the webroot doing nothing. The proof: these four headers have been
# declared here all along, and production sends none of them.
#
# The rules below are kept only as the declarative record of intent. The file
# that actually takes effect is deploy/nginx-napnix.conf — change both together,
# or delete this one once that config is live (see EDGE-CONFIG.md).
#
https://napnix.in/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
